# Cursor + Claude Rules

## Core behavior
- Read CLAUDE.md before making changes.
- Inspect existing code and conventions first.
- Make the smallest coherent change that satisfies the requirement.
- Do not invent APIs, packages, endpoints, schemas, or product behavior.
- Ask for clarification only when a missing decision blocks implementation; otherwise choose the simplest documented option and record the assumption.
- Never delete functional code without evidence.
- Never weaken security or validation to make a feature pass.

## Flutter
- Follow feature-first layered architecture.
- Keep domain independent from Flutter where practical.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Use null safety and explicit types.
- Prefer const widgets.
- Keep build methods cheap and deterministic.
- Do not perform I/O, networking, database work, or business calculations inside widgets.
- Reuse shared components and design tokens.
- Keep UI state separate from domain state.

## Business rules
- Centralize business rules in domain use cases/entities.
- Do not duplicate calculations for progress, streaks, achievements, or weekly compliance.
- Preserve historical records.
- Use normalized calendar dates for daily habit logic.
- Treat derived statistics as derived data, not the source of truth.

## Security
- Never add secrets to source control.
- Never log credentials, tokens, private reflections, or unnecessary personal data.
- Validate untrusted input.
- Use secure storage for sensitive client tokens.
- HTTPS only for remote APIs.
- Configure timeouts and controlled retries.
- Review dependency necessity before adding it.

## Tests
- Add or update tests when business behavior changes.
- Cover domain rules with unit tests.
- Cover important user flows with widget/integration tests.
- Do not remove tests to make CI pass.

## Git
- Use small focused commits.
- Suggested prefixes: feat, fix, refactor, test, docs, chore, security.
- Do not mix unrelated refactors with features.
- Before considering work complete:
  1. dart format --output=none --set-exit-if-changed .
  2. flutter analyze
  3. flutter test

## Review checklist
Before finalizing any change verify:
- architecture boundaries;
- business rules;
- null safety;
- error handling;
- security;
- tests;
- performance;
- documentation.

